This fish was probably born here, then headed out into the Pacific.

00:46:45.100 --> 00:46:48.600
Now, four years and thousands of miles later,

00:46:48.840 --> 00:46:52.300
it has returned to the very same stream to spawn.

00:46:57.140 --> 00:46:59.880
Salmon are very particular about where they lay their

00:47:00.030 --> 00:47:06.800
eggs and undergo an arduous trip inland against the current and the bears to find the right spot.

00:47:10.840 --> 00:47:21.030
And then, in the waters of their birth, they die. But reproduction is not quite the end of their

00:47:21.030 --> 00:47:27.640
contribution to the next generation. Their decaying bodies provide important nutrients for the fry

00:47:27.640 --> 00:47:29.810
that hatch, or at least

00:47:30.030 --> 00:47:32.370
those bodies that get a chance to decay.

00:47:38.510 --> 00:47:43.150
Even the wolves, habitual diners on red meat, turn up for a fish course.

00:47:54.220 --> 00:47:57.860
They've come to the easiest place for a wolf to catch a salmon.

00:48:05.470 --> 00:48:12.440
Their paws don't have the dexterity of a bear's and they can only capture a fish in extremely shallow areas.

00:48:45.580 --> 00:48:51.000
Our sitter has brought the pups, too, part of the preparation for the next phase of their training.

00:48:52.550 --> 00:48:58.710
As winter approaches, the pack will all join together again, and the pups will no longer be left behind.

00:49:13.500 --> 00:49:17.140
Soon, the bears will be finding dens to hibernate for the winter.

00:49:17.140 --> 00:49:20.850
But now, it's just time for a quick map.

00:49:30.480 --> 00:49:45.230
Our youngster will be facing his first winter without his mother's protection.

00:49:45.640 --> 00:49:49.600
Only the protection of the ravens, ancient decree.

00:50:04.190 --> 00:50:09.270
He's done quite well feeding himself and has already put on more than 50 pounds.

00:50:25.140 --> 00:50:29.660
But he will need lots of fat to get him through five months of hibernation.

00:50:30.540 --> 00:50:35.520
For a bear, one could possibly say it's survival of the fattest.

00:50:58.280 --> 00:50:59.760
At the end of the salmon season,

00:51:00.000 --> 00:51:01.720
The place to go is the coast.

00:51:03.880 --> 00:51:08.610
When the fish die, a lot of them are washed back down the streams to the sea.

00:51:09.260 --> 00:51:11.380
Now the gulls have their feast.

00:51:25.200 --> 00:51:29.980
There are prime spots here at the mouths of streams, but our bears not...

00:51:30.000 --> 00:51:38.800
the only one who knows about them. As usual, he'll have to compete for the right to fish

00:51:38.800 --> 00:51:59.490
here. He meets another bear who seems about his age and size.

00:52:05.560 --> 00:52:08.320
These two are extremely tolerant of each other.

00:52:08.710 --> 00:52:13.310
Rare behavior for black bears, especially when competing for food.

00:52:18.800 --> 00:52:22.940
All of his other encounters have been confrontations, but not this one.

00:52:34.480 --> 00:52:36.980
This lack of hostility is odd.

00:52:54.080 --> 00:52:56.380
They even seem to be playing a little.

00:53:04.800 --> 00:53:10.180
It's just possible that these two are siblings who've met up again after months apart.

